notes.content:
What's new in this update:

The board now adjusts to the number of players, avoiding excessively long matches;

Improved character graphics, colors, and animation tweaks;

Turn indicator for players;

Visual system improvements for color blindness;

Coming soon:

New Arena Mode (still in testing).

The classic dots and boxes game can now be played in a fun way with friends and family. In addition to the traditional mode, there’s the “Madness” mode, which adds items and new strategic possibilities. The game supports up to 5 players locally and offers the option to face a bot that simulates a child’s gameplay, with three difficulty levels — fun for all ages. The game also includes 20 achievements with varying difficulty levels and can be played remotely using Steam’s “Remote Play Together” feature.

What to expect in the future?
- New stages;
- Timed explosion mode;
- New char skins;
- New items;
- Story mode;
- Boss battle;
- and more...

Note: do not expect DLCs, every update will be included for free.
